  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building on Humane and Gender Inclusive Immigration and Border Management in ASEAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at ensuring human rights of all persons at international borders, including those who cross borders in irregular manners, and women in particular, are respected and protected. The goal will be achieved through enhancing border management capacity and partnership of ASEAN region and promoting gender mainstreaming at all levels of border security and management services. The project will directly benefit immigration and border management government officials, with a goal of over 40% of female officials from Cambodia, Indonesia, Lao PDR, the Philippines, Malaysia and Viet Nam. All ASEAN Member States citizens and foreigners crossing the selected ASEAN&apos;s borders will be indirect beneficiaries of the program.</narrative>
  </description>
